  "Question": "What is \\(\\dfrac{2^3 + 2^3}{2^{-3} + 2^{-3}}?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( 16 \\)",
    "B": "\\( 24 \\)",
    "C": "\\( 32 \\)",
    "D": "\\( 48 \\)",
    "E": "\\( 64 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "A negative exponent means taking the reciprocal, so\n\\[\n2^3=8,\\qquad 2^{-3}=\\frac1{2^3}=\\frac18.\n\\]\nThe denominator is \\(\\frac18+\\frac18=\\frac14\\), which is nonzero. Therefore\n\\[\n\\frac{2^3+2^3}{2^{-3}+2^{-3}}\n=\\frac{8+8}{\\frac18+\\frac18}\n=16\\div\\frac14\n=\\boxed{64},\n\\]\nchoice E.",
